  <content>
    <note class="self-check">
      <para>For the following exercise, consider this scenario: For each year \(t\), the population of trees in Forest A is represented by the function \(A(t)=115(1.025)^t\), (red curve). In a neighboring forest, Forest B, the population of the same type of tree is represented by the function \(B(t)=82(1.029)^t\), (blue curve). Looking at the graph provided, which forest had a greater number of trees initially?</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="GRAPH OF TWO EXPONENTIAL FUNCTIONS. THE FUNCTION A OF T IN RED HAS A \(y\)-intercepts OF 115. THE FUNCTION OF B OF T IN BLUE HAS A \(y\)-intercepts OF 82. ">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_09_04_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
    </note>
  </content>
</document>
